   <H1>[Python-ideas] JavaScript-Style Object Creation in Python (using a constructor function instead of a class to create objects)</H1>
    <B>Simon Ramstedt</B> 
    <A HREF="mailto:python-ideas%40python.org?Subject=Re%3A%20%5BPython-ideas%5D%20JavaScript-Style%20Object%20Creation%20in%20Python%20%28using%20a%0A%20constructor%20function%20instead%20of%20a%20class%20to%20create%20objects%29&In-Reply-To=%3CCAL0tCQEsOUG1wLuf984o%3DEk4_z77Lcmv7QWBuTM31mFdpQDUjg%40mail.gmail.com%3E"
       TITLE="[Python-ideas] JavaScript-Style Object Creation in Python (using a constructor function instead of a class to create objects)">simonramstedt at gmail.com
       </A><BR>
    <I>Sun May 14 00:07:44 EDT 2017</I>
    <P><UL>
        <LI>Previous message (by thread): <A HREF="045617.html">[Python-ideas] add a LogReader to the logging module
</A></li>
        <LI>Next message (by thread): <A HREF="045619.html">[Python-ideas] JavaScript-Style Object Creation in Python (using a constructor function instead of a class to create objects)
</A></li>
         <LI> <B>Messages sorted by:</B> 
              <a href="date.html#45618">[ date ]</a>
              <a href="thread.html#45618">[ thread ]</a>
